[00:06.63]It’s Sunday afternoon. What can I do?
[00:10.82]Annie 7 May
[00:14.08]It’s Sunday afternoon. The last hours of the weekend before school starts again.
[00:20.54]This time is valuable, but I’m sitting here with nothing to do and no money to spend!
[00:27.78]So I need ideas for things to do.
[00:30.48]Important: they need to be fun and free.
[00:34.98]I’m asking for help because time is running out!
[00:39.84]Austin08 (Five minutes ago)
[00:44.00]Go for a walk. I always go for a walk on Sunday. I like going on my own.
[00:52.29]It’s the perfect time to think about all the things I don’t normally have time to think about and I never think about things I need to do.
[01:00.59]I like forgetting all about them just for a few hours every week.
[01:08.02]MonsterMunch4342 (20 minutes ago)
[01:13.32]I’m writing my weekly poetry blog post. Well, I was – now I’m writing to you.
[01:21.58]I upload a post every Sunday.
[01:24.64]At the moment, I’m finishing poem number 15. Five more to go!
[01:30.70]Maybe you don’t want to write a poem or even a blog, so try a story.
[01:37.66]Go on – use your imagination!
[01:43.00]Cool656Carl (25 minutes ago)
[01:47.96]I’m lucky. I live in Liverpool and we have the best museums and they’re all free.
[01:55.81]They’re too big for just one visit, so one Sunday every month I go and check out a different room.
[02:04.21]Today it’s the insect room – I want to see what unusual bugs they have!
[02:11.68]SillyMilly (32 minutes ago)
[02:16.91]Read something. Sunday is my reading day.
[02:22.18]I read for at least four hours on a Sunday – books, magazines, websites, newspapers – anything.
[02:33.53]It’s free and best of all – you can do it anywhere.
[02:37.47]And sometimes, when I’m really lucky, Dad brings me a drink, too.
